2025-10-10 20:05:40,673 - evaluation_logger_Attraction-31 - INFO - Final Response: <|channel|>final<|message|>**Highest‑rated attraction in Madrid – Museo del Prado (Prado Museum)**  

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Name** | **Museo del Prado** (Prado Museum) |
| **Type** | Art museum / cultural landmark |
| **Typical rating** | 4.8 – 5.0 / 5 on TripAdvisor, Google Reviews, Booking.com, and other major travel sites |
| **Why it tops the list** | • Holds one of the world’s finest collections of European art (≈ 8 600 paintings).<br>• Consistently praised for its visitor services, audio‑guide options, and accessibility.<br>• Central location, easy to reach by public transport and close to other sights. |
| **Key highlights** | • Masterpieces by Velázquez, Goya, El Greco, Rubens, Titian, Bosch, and many more.<br>• Free entry on selected evenings (usually Monday‑Thursday 6 pm‑8 pm).<br>• Multilingual audio guides and private‑group tours available.<br>• Beautiful 19th‑century architecture and a tranquil garden courtyard. |
| **Practical info for a corporate group** | • **Group tours** – Private guided tours can be arranged for corporate groups (minimum 10‑15 people). Booking can be done online or through the museum’s sales office.<br>• **Location** – Plaza del Museo 1, 28014 Madrid. <br> • 5‑minute walk from Atocha train station; served by Metro (Lines 1, 3, 5 – “Atocha” stop).<br>• **Opening hours** – 10 am – 8 pm (Tue‑Sun); closed on Mondays (except holidays).<br>• **Accessibility** – Wheelchair‑friendly routes, elevators, and accessible restrooms.<br>• **Nearby amenities** – On‑site café, the Royal Botanical Garden, and the historic centre (Puerta del Sol, Plaza Mayor) are within walking distance. |
| **Suggested time slot** | Allocate **2–3 hours** (including a short coffee break). This fits nicely into a half‑day schedule, leaving the afternoon for a walking tour of the historic centre or a team‑building lunch. |

### Bottom line
For a corporate trip to Madrid, the **Museo del Prado** is the city’s highest‑rated attraction, offering an unforgettable cultural experience, excellent visitor facilities, and convenient logistics for groups. It makes an ideal centerpiece for your employee travel program.

